codex
The compiled summary rule was too specific: macro expansion coupled unrelated parts of the entire function configuration, so it never matched the live loop state. I’m tightening the lemma boundary to the loop itself. The proved invariant will summarize only `#while`, update `i` to `N`, and preserve the caller frame; ordinary reference-semantic rules then perform `return` and frame cleanup.
